{"content":[{"c":["ELIMELECH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Man from Bethlehem who took his wife, Naomi, and his sons, Mahlon and Chilion, to sojourn in Moab because of famine in Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.1.2-3","r":"Ruth.1.2-3","rawR":"Ruth.1.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.1.2-3","value":"Ruth.1.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ru 1:2-3"},"). While in Moab, he died; then his sons also died; and Naomi decided to return to Judah. One daughter-in-law, Orpah, preferred to remain in Moab; the other, Ruth, chose to accompany Naomi. Boaz, a kinsman of Elimelech, bought Elimelech’s land and married Ruth (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.9-10","r":"Ruth.4.9-10","rawR":"Ruth.4.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.9-10","value":"Ruth.4.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:9-10"},"). From this union came a great-grandson, David, and the royal line in which the Messiah would eventually be born. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=RuthBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"RuthBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"RuthBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ruth, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Elimelech","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ru 1:2-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.1.2-3","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.1.2-3","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.1.2-3"},{"anchorText":"4:9-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.4.9-10","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.4.9-10","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.4.9-10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7224318ba3cb9374449640f7681ab00fdf53c49529bcad9d060a5284d8146507","sourceItemName":"Elimelech","sourceItemOrder":105,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Elimelech","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Elimelech","title":"Elimelech","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}